# SQL DDL

Read @.ai/rules/sql-ddl.md before writing or changing PostgreSQL DDL. That file is the canonical DDL standard. Rules marked [lint] there are checked by `infrastructure/postgres/tests/ddl_lint.sql`.

- Every table and every column has a `COMMENT`. A column comment is a purpose sentence ending in a facts tag the lint compares to the catalog. History comments come from `topology.enable_versioning`, not from hand-written copies.
- Use lowercase `snake_case` and plural table names. Name constraints `pk_`, `uk_`, `ck_`, `fk_`, or `ex_`; indexes `ix_` or `ux_`; triggers `trg_`. Put units in the column name.
- Entity keys are `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`. Timestamps are `TIMESTAMPTZ` defaulting to `clock_timestamp()`. Use `JSONB`, lookup tables instead of `ENUM`, and no cross-schema foreign keys. A cross-module id is documented with `REF` and validated through the owning module's `.Contracts`.
- Scripts are re-runnable. Edited state is system-versioned; events reject `UPDATE` and `DELETE`. Follow section 9 of @.ai/rules/csharp-monolith.md.
- Write the pgTAP test first. Run `infrastructure/postgres/tests/run_tests.sh` before a pull request. Do not weaken the lint. Update `docs/architecture/data-model.md` in the same change.
